{"title":"1975 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A sequence of numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d745b81add053aa31f45d72cb9a898e3441e74bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, a_3, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> satisfies\n</p>\n<div class=\"ol\">\n<div class=\"li\"><span class=\"num\">(i)</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c93752fc9b032db99ff38f9114dcc254b098bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" /></div>\n<div class=\"li\"><span class=\"num\">(ii)</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2aa146d3f29ed75142daa3c1a4819df46b0582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_n=n^2a_n\\quad(n\\ge1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"284\" height=\"21\" /></div>\n</div>\n<p>Determine the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/0/1605df423a87f71177eb5e8eea50f6fbc9a8031a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n\\quad(n\\ge1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>I claim <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2fdec0b7a4ddf740744b60fef404c0789857c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\frac{1}{(n)(n+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"130\" height=\"43\" /> with a proof by induction. First we can use partial fraction decomposition to rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d211f086651908792faab3ca44222733a1c5ccb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{(n)(n+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"83\" height=\"41\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/d/4adc63840c2b04bc957f394f2de25658701bdd60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A}{n}+\\frac{B}{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"84\" height=\"39\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c5504b68076d2275f46436ea90f2a09fe0b85615.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{An+A+Bn}{(n)(n+1)}=\\frac{1}{(n)(n+1)}.\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"42\" /> We can set coefficients equal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b85afb2350833a45b60beb51bd83af087f95dd08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18428217dcd07944b2adbebcafd0978587a770a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901d0f8a1a66641048d9ccc607f9518f2ae64831.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{(n)(n+1)}=\\frac{1}{n}-\\frac{1}{n+1}.\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Base Case:</b> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db38177741a82f55d8162a7b207721c1f764f93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{(1)(1+1)}=\\frac{1}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"122\" height=\"41\" /> So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2fdec0b7a4ddf740744b60fef404c0789857c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\frac{1}{(n)(n+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"130\" height=\"43\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Inductive Step:</b> Suppose conclusion is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6fbf6b1b2bc81af471428fe2dc93cf475d6cd05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=k$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, such that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb885d08600a5d94f6db31d4f0d180511e808d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=\\frac{1}{k}-\\frac{1}{k+1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"127\" height=\"38\" /> We also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c97cd4f20a9db89ad7f0034237f417acb4481c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_k=k^2a_k.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"203\" height=\"17\" /> Add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/b/51bb8f97be092c275f4636c0782c3b93b3c69df8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> to both sides. The left side becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/a/8aa54f963be05e4a2af5eaf9968a65210d87958e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{k}-\\frac{1}{k+1}+a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"321\" height=\"38\" /> which is a telescoping series equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/266c2e5d91a873d6a826afebbdb3e0a0f2f70410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{k+1}+a_{k+1}=\\frac{k}{k+1}+a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"257\" height=\"39\" />. Now, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6fd0f288001b49a79d8dad1c8135decb39c0939.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_k+a_{k+1}=\\frac{k}{k+1}+a_{k+1}=(k+1)^2a_{k+1}.\\]\" width=\"448\" height=\"39\" /> We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/f/d9fe5d302a251df0f78c4121df50983a2ea722b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{k}{k+1}+a_{k+1}=(k+1)^2a_{k+1}\\implies \\frac{k}{k+1}=(k^2+2k+1-1)(a_{k+1}) \\implies \\left(\\frac{k}{k+1}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{(k)(k+2)}\\right)=a_{k+1} \\implies a_{k+1}=\\frac{1}{(k+1)(k+2)},\\]\" width=\"1005\" height=\"43\" /> thus the conclusion being true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6fbf6b1b2bc81af471428fe2dc93cf475d6cd05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=k$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, implies that it holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421df74ed1cff2239e3850e650dabfeb4663db9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />, so our induction is complete.<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Through manipulation, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/847548f5118205012b52968006b91bd002c02d4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_{n-1}=(n^2-1)a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"266\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62639f4f6b65d952c75776fa659c5a78b2bad60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_{n-1}=(n-1)^2a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"283\" height=\"21\" />. We divide the equations to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f89f1800af16c52f98205d7c5735c1d4cc3583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)a_n=(n-1)a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"193\" height=\"20\" />. This leads to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/a/a0a199e252210d6fe791ddffb6d994d96461d6ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {a_n}{a_{n-1}}=\\frac{n-1}{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"112\" height=\"42\" />. After that we can apply it all the way from n to 2 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf76e245397bf62024bd366e21c586ee60a0f0b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\frac{1}{2}*\\frac{1}{3}*\\frac{2}{4}\\cdots*\\frac{n-2}{n}*\\frac{n-1}{n+1}=\\frac{1}{n(n+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"365\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO\">1975 Canadian MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017171945\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 187/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 915/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6170/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.747      1 Template:Old_CanadaMO_box_(6-8_Problems)/8\n100.00%    6.747      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15102:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017171945 and revision id 288747. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}